      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — extracting a helper method to cut verbosity, adding a `@DisplayName`, and adding descriptive assertion messages that explain each case.The problem is the wildcard `?` on the helper return type — Java can't unify two separate `SimilarityInput<?>` captures into a single `E`. I need to make the helper generic.`COMPILE_OK`. The improved test compiles successfully. The key understandability improvements made:\n\n1. **Helper method `input()`** — replaces the verbose `SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, \"...\")` calls inline, making each assertion much easier to scan.\n2. **`@DisplayName`** — gives the test a human-readable description of its intent.\n3. **Assertion messages** — each `assertEquals` now carries a short label (e.g. `\"'frog' vs 'fog'\"`) so failures identify the broken case immediately.\n4. **Grouping comments** — brief comments before each block explain the *category* of the case (empty inputs, deletion, symmetry, etc.) without restating what the code already says."
    }
